<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Torstenson War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1643">1643</a>–<a href="/years/1645">1645</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Torstenson War of 1643–1645 was a conflict between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and Denmark-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> within <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War, named after the Swedish general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lennart-torstensson">Lennart Torstensson</a>, who invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jutland">Jutland</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Swedish forces also attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scania">Scania</a>, and a Swedish-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> fleet destroyed much of the Danish fleet at Fehmarn in 1644. By the Treaty of Brömsebro <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> ceded Gotland, Ösel, Jämtland and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harjedalen">Härjedalen</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/torstenson-war.jpg" alt="Torstenson War" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LocalF15 · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Torstenson_War_Collage.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
